    {
      "id": "lkXTvGYXnW4UDE0StYhb0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 838.6672624616729,
      "y": 893.1923285386517,
      "width": 499.3088684082031,
      "height": 381.2515716287047,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "8GTAbnmZZO-9BR6fEp8p1"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1X",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1589053556,
      "version": 2162,
      "versionNonce": 897637964,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785615652828,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- config timeout before new leader election begins\n- Data can be lost\n    - async replication\n    - leader node is in \"minority side\" of a network partition,\naccepts writes before failover\n\n- can use WAIT command for sync replication\n-  If replica fails, Redis cluster tries to\nget that master a new replica\n    - can preform full or partial resync to the master\n- should use at least RDB/AOF when using replication\n    - if not, master can fail and restart, while staying master\n    - ... its lost the data, so it will replicate empty\nstate to the replicas... everything becomes empty lol\n- evictions are performed by the master and sent to the replica\n- READ_ONLY commands can be handled by state replicas\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16.052697752787566,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- config timeout before new leader election begins\n- Data can be lost\n    - async replication\n    - leader node is in \"minority side\" of a network partition,\naccepts writes before failover\n\n- can use WAIT command for sync replication\n-  If replica fails, Redis cluster tries to\nget that master a new replica\n    - can preform full or partial resync to the master\n- should use at least RDB/AOF when using replication\n    - if not, master can fail and restart, while staying master\n    - ... its lost the data, so it will replicate empty\nstate to the replicas... everything becomes empty lol\n- evictions are performed by the master and sent to the replica\n- READ_ONLY commands can be handled by state replicas\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
